# Activates the flake's `devShells.default` on entering the directory.
#
# Guarded on `has nix`: a contributor without Nix gets a no-op instead of a
# direnv error on every `cd`. The flake is a convenience here, never a
# requirement — `cargo build` against a rustup toolchain at or above the
# `rust-version` in Cargo.toml is equally supported, and CI builds that way.
#
# `.gwm.toml` runs `direnv allow .` on bootstrap when this file exists, so a
# worktree created by `gwm create` picks the shell up without a manual step.
if has nix; then
  use flake
fi
